{"change_summary":"Bounded shrimp intake to one daily grazing budget by letting fine detritus backfill only unmet periphyton demand, aligned condition satiation with that single-source appetite basis, restored schema-3 `animal.reserve_g` migration by seeding reserve from legacy shrimp biomass, and updated shrimp/save regressions to cover the new feeding split, DO comparison, and reserve seeding behavior.","outstanding_risks":["Schema-3 reserve seeding is still heuristic: `reserve_g` is reconstructed from serialized adult and juvenile biomass because legacy saves did not store an explicit reserve pool.","The pre-existing untracked `.ralph-burning/` directory remains in the worktree and was left untouched."],"steps":[{"description":"Inspected the shrimp feeding and save-load paths, confirmed the intake-doubling and missing-reserve regressions, and chose a bounded-demand feeding fix plus legacy reserve reconstruction strategy.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Patched `shrimp_feeding` so periphyton consumes first and fine detritus only fills the remaining appetite, then updated the satiation target and added unit/integration coverage around the new feeding behavior.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Implemented schema-3 reserve migration from legacy shrimp biomass, updated save-load expectations, adjusted the dissolved-oxygen regression to compare fed vs unfed controls, and ran formatting plus targeted/full validation.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core shrimp_feeding_uses_detritus_only_for_unmet_demand` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test save_load legacy_schema_v3_saves_seed_reserve_from_existing_shrimp_biomass` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test shrimp_feeding_pathway` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core` passed."]}